// Trigger: the leaning stake at the river end of the palisade. Fires until
// depot_pass. At night a quiet person can get in here.
@speaker The river gap
=== start
[!night] -> day
The gap between the stakes is a shoulder wide and full of mud. On the other side, a lamp moves along the line of tents and stops, and moves again: the night watch, walking its round.
* [survival 40] Lie in the reeds and count the watchman's steps. Go when he turns. -> counted
* [roll sneak 0] Wait for the lamp to pass, then go through. -> through | seen
* [roll AGI -20] Go now, fast and low. -> through | seen
* Not tonight. -> END

=== day
In daylight the gap is obvious, and so is the watchman walking the line inside, and the sentries on the bluff who can see the whole riverbank. A thin person could get through here at night. Not now.
* Back off. -> END

=== counted
~ xp 25
Twenty-two steps to the forge, a pause to warm his hands, twenty-two back. He never looks at the river. Why would he? Nobody breaks into a prison.

On the twenty-third step, you go through.
-> inside

=== through
The mud takes you to the knee, the stake scrapes your back, and then you're inside, flat in the dark behind a tent, with the lamp going away from you.
-> inside

=== inside
~ set depot_pass; set depot_sneaked; xp 50
* Get up. -> END

=== seen
The lamp swings round. "Who's that?" A dog starts barking somewhere, then two. You're back through the gap and in the reeds before anyone with a spear gets there, but they'll be watching the river for a while now.
~ time 120
~ travel noviodunum reeds
